findings.body:
The aim was to drop a redundant `.clone()`, but the edit also changed the message variant from `DeleteCookie` to `SetCookie`:

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1712-1722"}

The event loop picks the wry call based on the variant (around line 3731). `SetCookie` goes to `webview.set_cookie(&cookie)`, so every call to `Webview::delete_cookie` / `WebviewWindow::delete_cookie` now sets or overwrites the cookie instead of removing it. For example, a logout flow that deletes a session cookie would leave it in place, which is also a security problem.

::callout{type="security"}
If an app relies on `delete_cookie` to clear auth or session cookies, those cookies stay set with no error and nothing logged.

The `WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie` variant and its handler at line 3737 are now never constructed.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1718-1718"}
        WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie(cookie.into_owned()),

The edited lines in `window_features` have extra spaces after one comma (`size.width,    size.height`) and none after the other (`position.x,position.y`). rustfmt will reject both if CI runs `cargo fmt --check`.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1315-1322"}

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1316-1322"}
    if let Some(size) = features.size() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.inner_size(size.width, size.height);
    }

    if let Some(position) = features.position() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.position(position.x, position.y);
    }

The swap so size is applied before position doesn't change behavior here, because the builder only stores both values. It does add noise to the diff, though.
